+# FINCH v2.12: go-live checklist
+
+## 1. Apply the patch
+Inside your project folder (the one containing App1.py):
+    patch -p1 < finch_v2.12.patch        # or just copy the files from the zip over yours
+    pip install -r requirements.txt
+    python -m pytest -q                  # all tests must pass before you deploy
+
+## 2. Environment / secrets
+Frontend (Streamlit): BACKEND_URL, BACKEND_SECRET_KEY, INVITE_CODE, ADMIN_EMAILS, SUPPORT_CONTACT (optional).
+Backend (FastAPI):    BACKEND_SECRET_KEY (same value), COHERE_API_KEY, optional AI_RATE_PER_HOUR, AI_DAILY_CAP.
+Both:                 FINCH_DB_PATH=/data/finch_v3.duckdb   <- must point at a PERSISTENT disk.
+Optional:             FINCH_SESSION_HOURS (default 72), FINCH_SPLASH=0 (turn the intro animation off).
+
+## 3. Persistent disk + backups (the #1 way to lose customers is to lose their data)
+- Most free hosts wipe local files on every deploy. Mount a persistent volume and set FINCH_DB_PATH to it.
+- DuckDB allows ONE writer process: run the Streamlit app as a single instance (do not scale to 2+ replicas).
+- Back up: log in as admin -> sidebar "Founder Admin Panel" -> "Back up database now" (writes Parquet files
+  under ./backups). Do it weekly at first and copy the folder off the server. Restore with:
+  DuckDB `IMPORT DATABASE 'backups/finch_backup_YYYYmmdd_HHMMSS'`.
+
+## 4. HTTPS and the session link
+Always serve over HTTPS (Streamlit Community Cloud, Render, Railway and Fly do this for you).
+Logged-in browsers keep a random 72-hour token in the page address (?s=...). It is revocable (Log out) and
+useless once expired, but anyone who is sent that exact link while it is valid is logged in. Tell users not to
+share their address bar. When you have time, swap it for a cookie-based session component.
+
+## 5. Password resets (no email server needed yet)
+User messages you -> admin panel -> "Generate reset code" -> send the 8-character code (valid 30 min) -> user uses the
+"Forgot password" tab. Codes are one-time and guess-limited.
+
+## 6. Known limits (be honest with pilot users)
+- AI rate limits live in the backend's memory and reset when it restarts. Fine for a pilot; use Redis later.
+- The database file is not encrypted at rest. The Privacy & Terms tab says so.
+- Have a Nigerian lawyer review the Privacy & Terms text against the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023 before you charge anyone.
+- Pricing/payment (Paystack/Flutterwave) is not built yet.
